plan_0:
- Consider pricing lower to match the competitor’s lowest prices to increase sales, but avoid going too low to maintain profitability;
   - Keep a close eye on the competitor's pricing strategy and be prepared to adjust my own price quickly if necessary;
   - Consider offering differentiating factors (e.g., quality, warranty, delivery times) to set myself apart from the competition.

insight_0:
- Aggressive pricing can help increase sales volume, but may not always result in higher profitability;
   - It is essential to stay aware of the competitor's pricing strategy and adjust accordingly;
   - Differentiating factors can help set myself apart from the competition and may lead to higher profit margins.
